"content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Dana Lee's trip is booked: the flight and the hotel are both confirmed, each booked once.\n\n- **Flight F100, SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, nonstop, $289** (reservation R0001). This was the cheapest nonstop. F120 costs $199 but has a stop, so I didn't pick it.\n- **Midtown Lodge in New York (H1), checking in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, $378 total** (reservation R0002). This was the cheapest hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card: $667.** That's under the $1,000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\nThe combined booking didn't go through cleanly. The first `book_trip` request timed out, so I retried it with the same request key to avoid booking twice. The system then said the original request had failed while reserving the hotel. Dana's reservations showed the flight had gone through and the hotel hadn't. I booked the hotel on its own, which is why the flight and hotel have separate reservation numbers.", "type": "text"}]}]}